window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Data-and-Functions--Constructors-with-Multiple-Parameters-_LPAR_Tuple-Types_RPAR_--Structures":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Data and Functions\u0009Constructors with Multiple Parameters (Tuple Types)","header":"2.1.9.1. Structures","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Data-and-Functions--Constructors-with-Multiple-Parameters-_LPAR_Tuple-Types_RPAR_--Structures"},"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--General-Proofs-about-Natural-Numbers--Displaying-Theorem-Statements":{"contents":"The #check command can also be used to examine the statements of\npreviously declared lemmas and theorems.\n\n#check mul_zero\n#check mul_succ\n\n\nNatPlayground.Nat.mul_zero (n : Nat) : n * zero = zero\n\n\nNatPlayground.Nat.mul_succ (n m : Nat) : n * succ m = n * m + n\n\n\n\n\nLean displays universally quantified variables as binders before the colon, which is\nthe preferred declaration-header style in Lean.\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Proof by Rewriting\u0009General Proofs about Natural Numbers","header":"2.2.8.1. Displaying Theorem Statements","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--General-Proofs-about-Natural-Numbers--Displaying-Theorem-Statements"},"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--The--injection--and--contradiction--Tactics":{"contents":"\n\nThe constructors of inductive types are injective (or one-to-one) and disjoint.E.g., for Nat:* if n + 1 = m + 1 then it must be that n = m* 0 is not equal to n + 1 for any n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Tactics: More Basic Tactics","header":"7.2. The  injection  and  contradiction  Tactics","id":"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--The--injection--and--contradiction--Tactics"}});